--
-- Description:
--
-- Note. This is the base test for all SPRAM random offload tests, and each SPRAM 
-- offload test is derived from this test, and will refer to this test.
--
-- The purpose of this test is to conentrate testing of small IPV4/TCP/UDP frames
-- with SPRAM operation. Small frames are the worst combination for SPRAM operation
-- as the percentage of writes per frame is higher - i.e. every frame has a
-- status word write, so as a percentage of a packet 1 status word will be
-- significant. This is apparent in SPRAM operation as the SPRAM is shared
-- between the read and write side, so a concentrated number of writes is more
-- difficult for the SPRAM solution. For a 64 byte packet there will be 4 data
-- writes (128b ram data width) and 1 status word write. IPV4/TCP/UDP packets are
-- particularly bad as the offload data is written at the end of a packet, so for
-- a 64 byte packet, the 64th byte is written, followed by IPV4 and TCP data, and 
-- then the status word, which equates to 4 writes in a row.
--
-- This tests applies a large number of 64-65 byte packets and ensures data
-- integrity. Other checkers within the system will ensure maximium
-- throughput, as this test has 0 idles and maximum throughput should
-- therefore be maintained.
--
-- Configuration:
--    1G mode
--    AHB/AXI random frequency - range between 1.5x to 8x.
--    AHB/AXI width - 64b
-- 
-- endDescription
--
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------


randomize_hready -descr_min 0 -descr_max 0 -data_min 0 -data_max 0
